    "summary": "Fixed KAFKA-19347: Unsafe state update in AclControlManager#createAcls\n\n**Problem**: The createAcls method was updating timeline data structures (idToAcl and existingAcls) before records were replayed, potentially exposing uncommitted state to callers.\n\n**Solution**: Modified the createAcls method to track deduplication locally using a Set<StandardAcl> instead of updating timeline structures. The fix:\n1. Added a local aclsInThisCall set to track ACLs added within the current call\n2. Changed the condition from `!existingAcls.contains(standardAcl)` to `!existingAcls.contains(standardAcl) && aclsInThisCall.add(standardAcl)`\n3. This ensures deduplication both within a single call and across calls without modifying timeline structures\n4. All timeline updates now happen exclusively through replay methods\n\n**Testing**: All 9 AclControlManagerTest tests pass, including testCreateDedupe which verifies proper deduplication within and across createAcls calls.\n\n**File changed**: metadata/src/main/java/org/apache/kafka/controller/AclControlManager.java"
  },
